              "databaseId": 72011,
              "author": { "login": "sam-r" },
              "body": "If two requests come in while the cache is empty (cold start, or right after expiry), both see no entry and both call `load()`, so we hit the catalog service twice. Under load that's a thundering herd on exactly the service this is meant to protect. Could we cache the in-flight promise instead of the resolved value, so concurrent callers share one load?",
              "url": "https://github.com/example/storefront/pull/420#discussion_r72011",
              "createdAt": "2026-11-18T13:40:19Z"
            }
          ]
        }
